# RAM Memory using Verilog

## Description

This project implements a synchronous RAM (Random Access Memory)
using Verilog HDL.

The RAM stores data at different memory addresses.

Configuration:

    Data Width  = 8 bits
    RAM Depth   = 16 locations
    Address     = 4 bits

Therefore, the RAM contains:

    16 x 8-bit memory locations

## Inputs

    clk       : Clock signal
    reset     : Reset signal
    we        : Write enable
    address   : Memory address
    data_in   : Data to be written

## Output

    data_out  : Data read from RAM

## Operation

### Write Operation

When:

    we = 1

data_in is written into the selected address.

Example:

    address = 3
    data_in = A5
    we = 1

The RAM stores:

    RAM[3] = A5

### Read Operation

When:

    we = 0

the data stored at the selected address is read.

Example:

    address = 3

Output:

    data_out = A5

## Files

    ram_memory.v
        RAM RTL design.

    tb_ram_memory.v
        RAM testbench.

    README.md
        Project documentation.

## Simulation

Compile:

    iverilog -o ram_tb ram_memory.v tb_ram_memory.v

Run:

    vvp ram_tb
